  "design_principles": [
    "Potable drinking-water, greywater, and roof-rainwater circuits are physically separate typed systems.",
    "Non-potable water is credited only for its admitted intended-use profile after an evidence-backed quality gate.",
    "Default safe state is physical bypass/isolation to an approved reject route.",
    "Gravity and passive process options are preferred only where a matched service and quality boundary supports them.",
    "All treatment modules remain candidates until source-property, challenge, process, residual and maintenance evidence is admitted.",
    "Storage sizing is derived from demand, admitted inflow, required autonomy, turnover and measurement uncertainty; no universal tank size is assumed.",
    "No software state, label or sensor alone substitutes for physical cross-connection prevention."
  ],
